Modifications in this application include: CLL/EG1/EG2 extraction; adding all
oriented-top cases; algorithm notation normalization; explicit starting setups,
final AUFs and cube-frame corrections; state-based matching of alternatives;
and correction of one source algorithm's case assignment.

Additional algorithm sequences were consulted from J Perm (Dylan Wang):
https://jperm.net/algs/2x2/cll
https://jperm.net/algs/2x2/eg-1
https://jperm.net/algs/2x2/pbl
Only move sequences and source identifiers are included; no site code or images
are included. Algorithms are mechanically verified. These sources do not endorse
this application. More detail and reproduction instructions: docs/SOURCES.md.

Square-1 OBL and Skewb NS2 catalogue data also incorporates the GPL-3.0
Alg-Trainers project by Malte Ihlefeld, at source snapshot:
3d19a613932319e33219105ad5bfd1f7a128ff24
Source directories: Sq1-OBL-Trainer, Sq1-CPEP-Trainer, Skewb-NS2-Trainer.
Changes include selecting OBL and NS2-only cases, preserving case/source IDs,
expanding notation, verifying alternatives, excluding invalid variants,
constructing equivalent setups, and generating original state-based diagrams.

Square-1 edge-permutation coverage and functional move sequences were consulted
from Sarah Strong's Square-1 EP collection:
https://sarah.cubing.net/square-1/ep
All 99 non-skip EP cases, including all 50 parity cases, are represented. No
source website code or diagram images are included. These sources do not
endorse this application. See docs/SOURCES.md for provenance and validation.
